  "term": "photoperiodism",
  "definition": "Photoperiodism is the way changes in day length act as a seasonal signal that helps regulate physiology and behavior. In the source packet, it refers to light information shaping biological timing through photoreceptors and clock-related processes so organisms synchronize with seasonal rhythms.",
